  "body": "From [process a navigate fetch](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#process-a-navigate-fetch), if a redirect response is encountered we end up with a `response` object that is the result of invoking [http-redirect fetch](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-http-redirect-fetch). From there we reach [process a navigate response](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#process-a-navigate-response), which takes us to the [page load processing model for HTML files](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#read-html). This says that \"Each task that the networking task source places on the task queue while fetching runs must then fill the parser's input byte stream\", which doesn't match the behaviour of responses returned from `http-redirect fetch`. In particular, that algorithm invokes [main fetch](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-main-fetch) with the recursive flag set, which causes an early return in step 13 to be taken. This means the the tasks that would be queued by the algorithm in steps 22, 24, and 27 will never be queued, so the parser will not get any content. ",
